  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Find the product $AB,$ if\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 & -2\\sqrt{6} \\\\ -1 & 7 & \\sqrt{6} \\\\ 5 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}]$\nand \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $AB=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that $B$ is the $3$rd *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ by the $3$rd *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3},$ the result must be the $3$rd *column* of $A.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nAB=[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{6} \\\\ \\sqrt{6} \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nLet's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 & -2\\sqrt{6} \\\\ -1 & 7 & \\sqrt{6} \\\\ 5 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4\\cdot 0+(-3)\\cdot 0+(-2\\sqrt{6})\\cdot 1 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot 0+7\\cdot 0+\\sqrt{6}\\cdot 1 \\\\ 5\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 0+(-8)\\cdot 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{6} \\\\ \\sqrt{6} \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
